# Wallfahrtskirche St. Wolfgang (back layer, no outlines, no figures, no
# text): the late-Gothic church seen from the lake side - whitewashed
# nave w/i with buttresses i/m and five tall pointed windows (b glass, d
# mullion, i frame, s glint), a steep slate roof m/d hipped over the
# choir (lit i ridge and hip), the square white tower with paired
# pointed belfry louvres (d/m), a clock face i/w/d without numerals and
# slit windows, under a bulbous onion helm m with a lit i left side and a
# d right side, a silver i knob and a slender m cross (never gold).
# Right: the courtyard wall with a pointed gate and two arcade arches
# (d) under a small m/d wall roof. The bottom row stands on the
# terrace's kalkfels top (row 11). 84 px tall: at the side camera's rest
# position the terrace top is 84 px below the screen top, so the whole
# silhouette with the onion and the cross stays on screen.
